# etude-5dr.5 plan — preserve the original run checkout

## Goal

Fix PR #22's blocking manifest-v4 provenance defect without changing the
caller-workspace guard: retain each caller stage's clean post-run `git_sha`, add
an immutable run-level `original_git_sha`, and make every operation that creates
a hermetic worktree use the original run checkout.

The defect is reproduced when stage 0 runs in the caller workspace and commits,
stage 1 fails, and resume checks out `stages[0].git_sha`. That field now names the
post-run commit, so the resumed hermetic stage silently runs against a different
tree than the fresh run. Single-stage replay, forward replay, replay recording,
and bench resolve the same stage-oriented SHA and have the same provenance error.

## Design

1. Extend manifest v4 with top-level `original_git_sha`. It is the immutable
   checkout selected when the run starts; caller stage `git_sha` remains the
   authoritative clean post-run HEAD. Version 0/2/3 manifests retain their
   historical meaning, where stage 0's `git_sha` is the run checkout.
2. Add one `Manifest.OriginalCheckout()` accessor that returns the v4 run-level
   value and falls back to stage 0 only for legacy versions. Require
   `original_git_sha` on v4 parse/write and reject it on versions below 4, so a
   malformed or pre-fix v4 manifest fails closed instead of silently choosing
   caller post-run provenance. Keep v0/v2/v3 serialized bytes unchanged.
3. Have live-run manifest writes carry the original `gitSHA` independently of
   each stage's post-run SHA. Resume uses `OriginalCheckout()` before creating
   its detached worktree; uninterrupted gate execution remains on the existing
   original worktree.
4. Have replay resolution expose both the selected stage provenance and the
   run's original checkout. Single-stage replay, forward replay, replay-record
   manifests, and bench checkout the original run SHA. The selected caller
   stage retains its post-run `GitSHA` for inspection rather than overwriting or
   relabeling it.
5. Update shipped run/replay/gate documentation to distinguish run-level
   original checkout from per-stage caller post-run provenance. Do not modify
   the separately owned bench documentation.

## Complete consumer set

- `internal/liverun/engine.go`: resume detached worktree.
- `internal/cli/replay.go`: single-stage replay detached worktree.
- `internal/liverun/replay_forward.go`: forward-replay detached worktree.
- `internal/bench/run.go`: benchmark replay detached worktree.
- `internal/replay/record.go`: recorded replay stage provenance must describe
  the checkout actually used.

`internal/replay.ResolveInputs` is the shared boundary for CLI replay, bench,
and replay recording, so it will return the original checkout explicitly while
preserving the embedded source stage and its post-run SHA.

## Compatibility and failure policy

- Manifests v0, v2, and v3 parse and replay exactly as before via stage 0.
- Hermetic-only live runs continue emitting v2/v3 with no new JSON field.
- Every newly emitted v4 manifest includes `original_git_sha`.
- A v4 manifest missing the field is rejected. Falling back to stage 0 for v4
  would recreate the reviewed silent-pass defect, so compatibility cannot take
  priority over provenance integrity on that malformed/unreleased shape.
- The existing caller dirty-tree and changing-HEAD guard stays at the same
  pre-publication point and retains all current tests.

